# Jaguar XF X260 four-door saloon, 2015-2024.
#
# The second XF: the aluminium-intensive body, the straighter shoulder
# crease, the flush door handles and the revised lamps. It went on sale in
# 2015 and ran to 2024.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XF_(X260)
#
# Dimensions 4.969 x 1.880 x 1.457 m, wheelbase 2.960 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation; the front and
# rear three-quarters show the lamps and tail.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the 2018 model year Jaguar XF UK brochure: Fuji White,
# Narvik Black, Indus Silver and Loire Blue. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total
# 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 250 km/h. Comfort 100/480, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 100. Class 2.
# Dates are road presence: 2015 intro, retires staggered 2036-2039.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-xf-x260.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-xf-x260.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-xf-x260/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the J-blade daytime light is not modelled, the grille is
# a flat panel, the twin exhausts are small chrome boxes and the wheels are plain
# discs. The rear window and boot are slightly longer than the photographs. At
# 128 px the longer cabin, swept lamps and large mesh grille read as an X260 XF.


